{"name":"Americana","hex":"#0477b4","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Americana","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["All things peculiar to the culture and people of the United States; anything that is a symbol of American life.","An amalgam of roots musics formed by the confluence of the shared and varied traditions that make up the American musical ethos; specifically those sounds that are merged from folk, country, blues, rhythm and blues, rock and roll and other external influential styles."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Americana"}],"entries":[{"title":"Americana","blocks":[{"text":"Americana artifacts are related to the history, geography, folklore, and cultural heritage of the United States of America. Americana is any collection of materials and things concerning or characteristic of the United States or of the American people, and is representative or even stereotypical of American culture as a whole."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Motherhood_and_apple_pie.jpg/330px-Motherhood_and_apple_pie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Americana","wikidata":"Q467355"},{"title":"Americana (The Offspring album)","blocks":[{"text":"Americana is the fifth studio album by American rock band The Offspring, released on November 17, 1998, by Columbia Records. Following a worldwide tour in support of Ixnay on the Hombre (1997), the band commenced work on a new album in July 1998, with the recording sessions lasting for about two months. It was The Offspring's second and last album to be produced by Dave Jerden."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f5/TheOffspringAmericanaalbumcover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Americana_(The_Offspring_album)","wikidata":"Q179137"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedi